   "id": "hysteresis",
   "title": "Comparator with hysteresis",
   "page": 8,
   "description": "The signal drives -IN directly. R1 from VREF and R2 from OUT meet at +IN, so the output pulls the +IN threshold up or down and the switching point moves between VHI and VLO, centred on VREF. The window width is set by R1 / (R1 + R2). CF, across R2, is optional: above fP = 1 / (2π CF R2) it widens the window towards VHI = V+ - 1 V and VLO = 0 V, which helps a slow input in high-frequency noise.",
